    "text": "To determine the cost per person for the New Year’s Eve appetizer, we need to calculate the total cost of the ingredients and then divide by the number of people the appetizer will serve.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total cost of the potato chips:\n- Alex buys 3 individual bags of potato chips, each costing $1.00.\n\\[\n3 \\text{ bags} \\times \\$1.00 \\text{ per bag} = \\$3.00\n\\]\n\nNext, we add the cost of the creme fraiche:\n- The creme fraiche costs $5.00.\n\\[\n\\$3.00 + \\$5.00 = \\$8.00\n\\]\n\nThen, we add the cost of the caviar:\n- The caviar costs $73.00.\n\\[\n\\$8.00 + \\$73.00 = \\$81.00\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the cost per person. The appetizer will serve 3 people, so we divide the total cost by 3:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\$81.00}{3 \\text{ people}} = \\$27.00 \\text{ per person}\n\\]\n\nThus, the cost per person for the appetizer is \\(\\boxed{27}\\).",
